# Conditions of one type each are no class A: in peek, `k = 5 && j = 5U` joins an int comparison and a size_t one (each
# is its own condition; `&&` gives an int), and `(cast: (size_t) k) = j` is one type.  k is the caller's free name, so
# the first condition waits for its type (kind 3) and passes.  3 + 4: Entry 7.
fn: peek () int
    size_t: j 5U
    int: out 0
    if: k = 5 && j = 5U
        out: out + 3
    if: (cast: (size_t) k) = j
        out: out + 4
    int: r out
    return: r
fn: m () int
    int: k 5
    return: peek()
int: code 0
code: m()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
